  "bounds": "150 managed cases/groups passed using injected capture/time/network and isolated child processes. Recovery includes an actual hidden synthetic child with ten-second startup delay, pause inheritance and isolated singleton acquisition; GUI crash paths remain source-reviewed. Owner confirmed physical lock/off/resume and automatic Windows display-off/resume on0.1.1, whose capture, color, network and display-notification code is unchanged. No full system-sleep or long-duration physical acceptance for0.1.2. Native DLL unchanged.",
  "changes": "Adds durable lifecycle and queued power diagnostics, persisted display/standby state, serialized local logging and bounded same-EXE hidden relaunch after caught managed failures. Three retries, ten-second delay, budget reset after ten minutes; runtime pause preserved; explicit Exit/Windows shutdown suppress recovery. No scheduled-task mechanism or watchdog. Does not recover force termination or uncatchable native faults. Existing sampling, zones, off/wake commands and defaults unchanged from0.1.1."
